  "method": "Alignment-free half-probe hashing and tag-aware cell calling, using the accepted RAM bucket mode and full 32-thread permit budget. JAX and GSE325982 local reader variants and all six delivered-FASTQ/CBQ arms on each cloud storage class are included. CBQ preparation is excluded. Bootstrap stream settings are preserved. A multiplexed cell remains the barcode plus sample tag; pooled cell concordance and sample means are distinct, and off-target JAX tags remain in the all-tag call-set comparison. Local walls are GNU time driver intervals; cloud walls use the accepted measurement wrapper through process exit, with GNU time separately retained. The corrected 1.9.5 tag was built with the accepted benchmark recipe and one SHA256-identified binary was used everywhere. Scientific arguments, input formats, reference content, hash caches, and caller settings were preserved. Each arm ran once on a quiet host, with fresh outputs and a fatal cold-cache preflight. All input, reference, output, temporary and spill locations were checked against the intended storage. Comparator outputs and times were retained; no comparator was rerun. Completion, executed-command identity, the 1.30 maximum timing ratio, and canonical correlation/cell-call tolerances were checked before scheduling the next arm. Byte equality is a recorded diagnostic rather than an acceptance gate. Untimed cloud concordance calculations are reused only when all matrix components, method code and validation dependency versions have identical checksums; changed inputs compute fresh metrics. Each arm retains its own report and every numeric gate.",
